   {
    "title": "Senior System On a Chip Design Project",
    "description": "Semester long hardware development project to create a fully functional system-on-a-chip deployed in a Xilinx FPGA. The SoC includes a self-developed UART capable of communicating on a range of baud rates from 300 to 921600 bits/sec, and a 16-bit emulator of the Xilinx PicoBlaze processor developed by the course instructor.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Mar 2016 - May 2016"
   },
   {
    "title": "Senior Embedded Systems Project",
    "description": " 4-week project to develop a system capable of interfacing two ARM systems utilizing the mbed RTOS. Final functionality includes a 5-axis joystick and MMA7455 accelerometer to control LEDs located on both development boards. Board to board communication is achieved through SPI, board to PC communication achieved through UART serial communication.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Nov 2015 - Dec 2015"
